WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.544 --> 00:00:04.306
"You look hungry and tired," the prince said to Tom.

2
00:00:04.326 --> 00:00:05.706
"Come with me."

3
00:00:05.726 --> 00:00:07.587
Tom was stunned by what was happening.

4
00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:14.250
The prince led him through the palace until they came to the prince's room.

5
00:00:31.616 --> 00:00:35.299
While the prince ordered breakfast for his guest, Tom looked around.

6
00:00:35.319 --> 00:00:40.763
"Imagine sleeping in that big bed instead of on the floor!"

7
00:00:41.223 --> 00:00:41.883
Tom thought.

8
00:00:41.903 --> 00:00:51.670
"He has so many books and a suit of armor and—" "What's your name and where do you

9
00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:54.932
live?" The prince interrupted Tom's thoughts.

10
00:00:56.253 --> 00:00:58.255
"I'm Tom Canty from Offal Street.

11
00:00:58.795 --> 00:00:59.596
And who are you?"

12
00:01:01.792 --> 00:01:02.913
"Prince Edward."

13
00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:06.516
"Prince Edward!

14
00:01:06.856 --> 00:01:09.599
You mean, King Henry's son and heir?"

15
00:01:12.021 --> 00:01:14.703
The prince nodded, and Tom quickly bowed.

16
00:01:14.723 --> 00:01:18.606
"I'm sorry to hear that the king is ill.

17
00:01:19.607 --> 00:01:21.008
Everyone is talking about him.”

18
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.231
"I fear that my father may die soon.

19
00:01:26.693 --> 00:01:30.616
Some people say he's cruel, but he has always treated me fairly."

20
00:01:32.084 --> 00:01:33.865
The prince paused and smiled.

21
00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:36.405
"Though he does like to criticize me."

22
00:01:36.425 --> 00:01:39.906
"My father is mean to everyone!"

23
00:01:40.286 --> 00:01:40.986
Tom said.

24
00:01:42.607 --> 00:01:46.628
Just then Tom's meal arrived, and he dug in with both hands.

25
00:01:51.049 --> 00:01:59.551
"He has no table manners," Prince Edward thought, "and yet "You speak as though you've had some education,"

26
00:02:00.032 --> 00:02:01.192
the prince said to Tom.

27
00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:06.343
"Yes, I can read and write, but I struggle with Latin."

28
00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:10.626
"Latin is hard at first," the prince said.

29
00:02:10.646 --> 00:02:12.787
"But enough about studying.

30
00:02:13.748 --> 00:02:16.030
Is it pleasant to live on Offal Street?"

31
00:02:18.151 --> 00:02:21.894
Tom thought about the poor families who crowded together in every house.

32
00:02:21.914 --> 00:02:26.357
"Sometimes it is, but not when we're hungry."

33
00:02:28.079 --> 00:02:29.740
He gobbled up some ham and eggs.

34
00:02:31.508 --> 00:02:33.389
"I hope that doesn't happen too often.

35
00:02:34.629 --> 00:02:35.650
Do you have any friends?

36
00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:37.310
What do you like to do?"

37
00:02:38.851 --> 00:02:40.232
Tom swallowed some bread.

38
00:02:40.252 --> 00:02:44.593
"My friends and I are always racing to see who's the fastest."

39
00:02:45.794 --> 00:02:47.035
"Oh, I'd like that!"

40
00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:48.215
the prince said.

41
00:02:48.235 --> 00:02:53.697
"People say I'm a good runner, but I don't have anyone to compete against.

42
00:02:54.938 --> 00:02:59.980
My only friends are my older sister, Princess Elizabeth, and my cousin, Lady Jane.

43
00:03:01.432 --> 00:03:02.972
What else do you do with your friends?"

44
00:03:02.992 --> 00:03:06.533
"In summer we swim in the river.

45
00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:09.854
We shout and splash each other with water.

46
00:03:10.855 --> 00:03:14.576
Of course, that's after we've played in the mud and made mud pies!"

47
00:03:18.757 --> 00:03:21.958
not allowed to get wet outdoors," the prince said sadly.

48
00:03:21.978 --> 00:03:24.878
"Then how do you get clean?"

49
00:03:25.299 --> 00:03:26.159
Tom asked.

50
00:03:26.179 --> 00:03:30.260
"I have many servants who help me bathe."

51
00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:33.854
The prince sighed.

52
00:03:33.874 --> 00:03:36.577
"Your life sounds wonderful.

53
00:03:38.078 --> 00:03:42.882
If I could run barefoot in the mud, I'd give up my right to be king!"

54
00:03:42.902 --> 00:03:45.564
Tom was horrified.

55
00:03:45.584 --> 00:03:48.086
"You can't do that, sir!

56
00:03:48.867 --> 00:03:50.528
Besides, it's not all fun.

57
00:03:50.548 --> 00:03:56.633
On New Year's Day, my best friend, Julian, fell into the river and almost drowned.

58
00:03:57.774 --> 00:03:59.456
Luckily, a stranger saved him."

59
00:04:01.472 --> 00:04:05.496
"I'm sorry to hear about Julian, but I wish I could play with your friends."

60
00:04:05.516 --> 00:04:11.461
"And I wish I could be a prince, if only for one day."

61
00:04:11.481 --> 00:04:15.844
"Would you really like that?"

62
00:04:16.265 --> 00:04:17.386
the prince asked.

63
00:04:18.947 --> 00:04:19.908
Tom nodded.

64
00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:23.871
Prince Edward grinned.

65
00:04:23.891 --> 00:04:25.773
"Then let's do it!

66
00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:32.077
We'll trade clothes for a while and then switch back before anyone finds out."

67
00:04:34.878 --> 00:04:40.821
A few minutes later, the prince was wearing Tom's rags, and Tom was dressed in the prince's fine

68
00:04:40.881 --> 00:04:46.343
garments. The two boys stood side by side in front of a large mirror.

69
00:04:47.404 --> 00:04:51.325
They stared at each other, then at the mirror, then at each other again.

70
00:04:51.345 --> 00:04:56.047
"We look so much alike," Edward whispered.

71
00:04:58.400 --> 00:04:59.720
Tom laughed nervously.

72
00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:03.121
"We do indeed, sir."

73
00:05:03.141 --> 00:05:09.083
"Except Edward frowned, peering at Tom's hand.

74
00:05:09.103 --> 00:05:13.024
"You have a bruise where that guard grabbed your hand."

75
00:05:13.044 --> 00:05:15.765
"It's nothing."

76
00:05:16.225 --> 00:05:18.046
Tom hid his hand behind his back.

77
00:05:18.066 --> 00:05:20.446
"It was cruel!"

78
00:05:21.987 --> 00:05:23.447
The prince stamped his foot.

79
00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:26.348
"Now close your eyes.

80
00:05:27.564 --> 00:05:30.206
I need to put away something important before I leave."

81
00:05:33.388 --> 00:05:34.289
Tom didn't peek.

82
00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:39.152
He imagined that Edward was hiding documents—or even jewels.

83
00:05:42.855 --> 00:05:44.256
done!" Edward said.

84
00:05:44.276 --> 00:05:47.618
"Don't move until I return to this room.

85
00:05:48.819 --> 00:05:49.580
That's a command!"

86
00:05:51.281 --> 00:05:55.144
Tom stood still while Edward rushed from the room and out to the courtyard.

87
00:05:57.668 --> 00:05:59.069
"Open this gate at once!"

88
00:05:59.629 --> 00:06:00.869
Edward shouted to the guard.

89
00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:04.091
The guard hurried to open the gate.

90
00:06:05.291 --> 00:06:08.613
But as Edward passed by, the guard knocked him to the ground.

91
00:06:08.633 --> 00:06:11.674
"You wretched pauper!

92
00:06:12.314 --> 00:06:15.095
Because of you, I got a scolding from Prince Edward!"

93
00:06:16.896 --> 00:06:19.717
Edward's face flushed with anger as he picked himself up.

94
00:06:19.737 --> 00:06:23.338
"I'm Prince Edward!

95
00:06:24.219 --> 00:06:28.101
When I return, you'll be locked up for hurting me—and my friend!"

96
00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:33.245
The guard sneered and gave Edward a mock salute.

97
00:06:33.265 --> 00:06:37.469
"I salute Your Gracious Highness.

98
00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.111
Now get out of here!"

99
00:06:41.712 --> 00:06:46.096
A few people were still waiting outside the gate, hoping for a glimpse of royalty.

100
00:06:50.099 --> 00:06:52.941
They laughed and shouted.

101
00:06:52.961 --> 00:06:55.864
"Make way for His Royal Highness!"

102
00:06:56.374 --> 00:06:57.042
they cried.
